						<!--<p class="pepper">layout/blocks/body/_footnotes</p>-->
<div class="container py-5 fade-in">
	<div class="row">
		<div class="max-w-2xl lg:w-10/12 mx-auto text-sm wysiwyg">
			<p><em>*</em> Global: large organisations who are engaged in most or all major financial centres around the world. <br />** Regional: for all other organisations that conduct business primarily within their own country and/or region. <br />*** SME/Services: for small to medium sized enterprises (SMEs), not for profits and small consulting firms. </p>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
      					
						
<!--<p class="pepper">layout/blocks/body/_text</p>-->


		<div class="container py-5 fade-in">
	<div class="row">
						<div class="max-w-2xl lg:w-10/12 mx-auto wysiwyg ">
						<h2>Subscriber status</h2>
<p><span dir="ltr">Subscribers do not form part of LBMA’s membership and therefore do not have the same voting rights as Members and do not benefit from the Terminal Markets Order. Subscribers are also not permitted to use the LBMA logo or branding.</span></p>
<h2>Application process</h2>
<ol><li><strong>Apply</strong>: Submit an application by contacting our Membership team using the button below.</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: LBMA sets and maintains high standards of integrity so all applications are subject to a due diligence process.</li><li><strong>Approve</strong>: the LBMA Executive Committee considers the application for approval.</li><li><strong>Subscribe</strong>: once an application has been approved, Subscribers are notified and invoiced their respective fees. On payment, LBMA’s membership services coordinator will make contact to start the on-boarding process.</li></ol>
		</div>
        	</div>
</div>
								
						


	
